      "content": "That's very helpful for the mood boards. \n\nI want to dig a bit deeper into the \"vibe\" for the design team. When we're talking about the \"Heritage\" look, it seems like it's inherently linked to a very specific type of white, Eurocentric standard of beauty and decorum. On the flip side, the \"Urban\" profile you described seems to lean heavily into more racialized or \"ethnic\" tropes. \n\nCould you explain why these two categories—refined/legacy vs. trendy/street—end up being so strictly divided along those racial and ethnic lines? Is it just a matter of where the money comes from, or is there something more fundamental about the cultural \"essence\" of each group that dictates their aesthetic?",
